{"id": "EUVD-2026-103866", "enisaUuid": "1b96e413-bcb5-3384-80bb-e182015687c5", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/mediatek: Fix pdev reference leak in mtk_drm_bind()\n\nWhen the device is not the mmsys master, mtk_drm_bind() returns early\nafter taking a reference on the disp-mutex device via\nof_find_device_by_node(), without ever dropping it: mtk_drm_unbind()\nonly puts mutex_dev for the master. Drop the reference before returning\nfrom the non-master path.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:48:18", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:56:55", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4a0ae61067671f556eeaf5ea4e59a1db63163d70", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4a8f9cad0fced77b36b297c67c42730c9cb32ec6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b84f1386d84b3a73f73ebb416a3f97c5d64a8ab3", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/cb3e0244514d13507c6048777e1d0277e611cf6c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3753e34b73fcbe2a2edbe984614a008a261697ef"], "aliases": ["GHSA-3r3h-q9jp-47gf", "CVE-2026-98781"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1a7dec2c-7f45-3ea1-b514-5024ea1aa781", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1ef7ed48356cd5f9af2b7671956991b658d8c2ba <4a8f9cad0fced77b36b297c67c42730c9cb32ec6"}, {"id": "39b891d4-b463-324b-b036-fe0296d51634", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "4c8f3686-38d2-3b59-b99e-10da7ee13d48", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1ef7ed48356cd5f9af2b7671956991b658d8c2ba <cb3e0244514d13507c6048777e1d0277e611cf6c"}, {"id": "5d1fc509-c9e7-3c34-b7e0-17031ba9b290", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.4"}, {"id": "5e86e7d4-a385-3a51-8602-37d6d7610e62", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.10"}, {"id": "6b9725f3-5e9e-39f8-a573-af3d0